Track 3: Isla Maciel Spark-Gap
- Story & Context: By the time the squall of 1994 collapsed the pirate transmitter mast atop the Isla Maciel salt warehouse into the Riachuelo, the band had vanished into urban folklore, leaving behind only muddy boot prints and scorched vacuum tubes. Scrap dealers combing the low-tide marshes recovered an organ volume pedal encrusted with saltpetre and a torn bandoneon reed that still hummed when the wind whipped through the reeds. Dock elders maintain that during October squalls, if you touch a brass pocketknife to the iron girders of the ferry bridge, Corvalán's voice cuts through the thunder howling, "The storm never asks whose house it breaks." The track stands as an incendiary monument to a radio station that lived and died by atmospheric discharge.
